event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":97,"item_id":"rs_0c30853fdc2e871b016ac952e0c96087d189efb2e514bc99b1","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing server functionality**\n\nI’m considering how to create a clean, small server that utilizes HTML Server-Side Rendering (SSR) with forms, including validating inputs and handling errors like HTTP 400. I want to use POST redirection for safety and ensure proper escaping for headings. Also, I’m thinking about generating UUIDs with SQLite and organizing data efficiently. Plus, modular CSS for page rendering sounds like a good idea. I’m curious if 8k tokens would be ample for this project!"}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":98,"item_id":"rs_0c30853fdc2e871b016ac952e0c96087d189efb2e514bc99b1","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing server functionality**\n\nI’m considering how to create a clean, small server that utilizes HTML Server-Side Rendering (SSR) with forms, including validating inputs and handling errors like HTTP 400. I want to use POST redirection for safety and ensure proper escaping for headings. Also, I’m thinking about generating UUIDs with SQLite and organizing data efficiently. Plus, modular CSS for page rendering sounds like a good idea. I’m curious if 8k tokens would be ample for this project!"}}

